course: dictionary
lesson: 5051
title: Inquest: finding out why
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An inquest is a formal inquiry, a careful search for the reasons something happened. In law, a coroner leads an inquest when a person dies suddenly or in a way nobody can explain. The words around it give clues: «At the Hillsborough disaster in 1989, 97 Liverpool fans died in a crush» tells you something terrible happened, so an inquest is a serious look at what went wrong.
explain: The word also has an informal meaning: a long discussion after something has gone wrong. If a team loses badly and the players spend an hour talking about every mistake, that is a post-match inquest. Check by swapping in "a careful look at why": the meaning still fits.
explain: Notice the phrases around the word: hold an inquest, the coroner's inquest, an inquest into something. These are common in news reports, so spotting them helps you read the news.
fact: An inquest is an official inquiry, usually led by a coroner.
fact: An inquest tries to find out why and how a person died, especially when the death was sudden or unexplained.
fact: «Inquests in 2016 found they were unlawfully killed» shows that inquests can change what people understand about the past.
fact: Informally, an inquest is a long discussion after something has gone wrong, such as a lost match.
fact: Phrases to remember: hold an inquest, the coroner's inquest, an inquest into something.
exercise: A coroner will hold an inquest into the sudden death. What is an inquest? | A cake shop | A type of hospital bed | *An official inquiry to find out why and how a person died | A quiet holiday
exercise: After the team lost 5-0, the coach held a long talk to find out what went wrong: a post-match inquest. What does inquest mean here? | *A long discussion to find out why something went wrong | A short, happy goodbye | A new team kit | A prize for winning
exercise: Which phrase is a common way to say that a formal inquiry is being held? | sing a song | *hold an inquest | make a cake | run a race
test: «The inquest into the accident heard from twelve witnesses.» What is the best meaning of inquest? | A party | *A formal inquiry | A race
test: After the school play went badly, the class had an inquest about what went wrong. What does inquest mean here? | *A long discussion to find out why something went wrong | A costume | A quiet nap | A celebration
exam: Which explanation of inquest is best? | A word for a sudden storm | A type of football match | A kind of old castle | *An official inquiry, or a long discussion, to find out why something happened
